      "name": "StringPrefixMatchCaseInsensitive",
      "signature": "int StringPrefixMatchCaseInsensitive(char * lpszString, char * lpszPrefix)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive prefix match comparing if lpszPrefix is at the start of lpszString.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute strlen(lpszString) using SCASB.REPNE\n2. Compute strlen(lpszPrefix) using SCASB.REPNE\n3. If strlen(lpszString) < strlen(lpszPrefix), return -1 (string too short)\n4. Compute strlen(lpszPrefix) again for loop counter\n5. Loop through each character of lpszPrefix:\n   a. Convert current char of lpszString to uppercase via ToUpper helper\n   b. Convert current char of lpszPrefix to uppercase via ToUpper helper\n   c. If characters differ, return comparison result (-1 or 1)\n   d. Advance both pointers\n   e. Decrement counter, continue if not zero\n6. If loop completes (all prefix chars matched), return 0\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString - char * - Input string to check for prefix (ECX, __fastcall)\n  lpszPrefix - char * - Prefix string to search for (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  0  - lpszPrefix matches start of lpszString (case-insensitive)\n  -1 - lpszString is shorter than lpszPrefix OR first mismatch is less-than\n  1  - First mismatch character is greater-than\n\nCallers: FUN_6fa06290 (command parser) uses this for /d2notify command matching\n\nRegister Usage:\n  EBP - Pointer to current char in lpszString\n  ESI - Pointer to current char in lpszPrefix  \n  EBX - Remaining characters to compare (loop counter)\n  EDI - Temporary for strlen computation, then comparison result",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:5611e702fb25e719faaecb561321a0e9ee8f62537972b9ec1f4c2012a0d6b5e6",
