      "comment": "Adjusts the Battle.net list scroll position by a delta and updates scroll arrow UI states.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Core scroll position management for Battle.net list UI\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current scroll position in dwPreviousScrollPosition for change detection\n2. Initialize scroll arrow flags (nCanScrollUp, nCanScrollDown) to 0 (disabled)\n3. Check if content is scrollable (lineCount >= 12 visible lines):\n   - If fewer than 12 lines: Reset scroll position to 0, skip to step 8\n   - Calculate dwMaxScrollPosition = lineCount - 11 (visible window size)\n4. Calculate new position = currentPosition + nScrollDelta\n5. Clamp position to valid range [0, dwMaxScrollPosition]:\n   - If newPosition < 0: Clamp to 0 via bitwise AND trick\n   - If newPosition > dwMaxScrollPosition: Clamp to max\n6. Set nCanScrollUp = 1 if scrollPosition > 0 (can scroll toward top)\n7. Set nCanScrollDown = 1 if scrollPosition < dwMaxScrollPosition (can scroll toward bottom)\n8. If position changed: Call FUN_6fa0b4d0 to re-render list items\n9. Update scroll arrow UI objects via SetUnitBitMask:\n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[0xB]: Up arrow primary (uses nCanScrollUp)\n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[0xC]: Down arrow primary (uses nCanScrollDown)\n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[0xD]: Up arrow secondary (uses nCanScrollUp)\n   - g_apBnetUIObjects[0xE]: Down arrow secondary (uses nCanScrollDown)\n\nParameters:\n  nScrollDelta (int, ECX): Scroll amount - positive scrolls down, negative scrolls up\n                          Common values: 1/-1 (single line), 10/-10 (page), -1 (scroll to top)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_dwAutomapScrollPosition (0x6fa21aa0): Current scroll position (READ/WRITE)\n  g_dwAutomapLineCount (0x6fa21a9c): Total line count in list (READ)\n  g_apBnetUIObjects[0xB-0xE]: Scroll arrow UI objects (READ for pointer)\n\nCallees:\n  FUN_6fa0b4d0: Re-renders visible list items after scroll position change\n  SetUnitBitMask: Updates UI object visibility/state flags\n\nCallers:\n  ScrollAutomapUp (0x6fa01f10): Passes delta=10 for page-up scroll\n  ScrollBnetListUp (0x6fa01f30): Passes delta=-1 for scroll-to-top\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xB (11): Visible lines in scroll window\n  0xC (12): Minimum lines needed for scrolling to be enabled\n  0xB-0xE: UI object indices for scroll arrows (up/down pairs)\n\nClamping Logic (bitwise trick at 0x6fa0a977-0x6fa0a97f):\n  Uses SETLE/DEC/AND to clamp negative values to 0:\n  - SETLE CL: Sets CL=1 if newPos <= 0, else CL=0\n  - DEC ECX: CL=1 becomes 0, CL=0 becomes -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n  - AND EAX,ECX: If newPos was negative, mask is 0, result is 0",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
