      "name": "IsValidNameCharacter",
      "signature": "bool IsValidNameCharacter(uint dwUnused1, uint dwUnused2, char * lpszCharacter)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates if a character is allowed in player/game names.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read character from input string pointer\n2. Check if character is special allowed char (space, apostrophe, hyphen, underscore)\n3. If special char, return true (valid)\n4. Check if character is digit ('0'-'9', ASCII 0x30-0x39)\n5. If digit, return true (valid)\n6. Check if character is uppercase letter ('A'-'Z', ASCII 0x41-0x5A)\n7. If uppercase, return true (valid)\n8. Check if character is lowercase letter ('a'-'z', ASCII 0x61-0x7A)\n9. If lowercase, return true (valid)\n10. Otherwise, return false (invalid character)\n\nParameters:\ndwUnused1 [uint, Stack+0x4]: Unused parameter (callback signature compatibility)\ndwUnused2 [uint, Stack+0x8]: Unused parameter (callback signature compatibility)\nlpszCharacter [char*, Stack+0xC]: Pointer to single character to validate\n\nReturns:\ntrue (1): Character is valid for name input\nfalse (0): Character is not allowed\n\nValid Characters:\nSpace (0x20), Apostrophe (0x27), Hyphen (0x2D), Underscore (0x5F)\nDigits 0-9 (0x30-0x39)\nUppercase A-Z (0x41-0x5A)\nLowercase a-z (0x61-0x7A)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses switch/jump table for special characters (optimized comparison)\nFirst two parameters are unused - likely callback signature compatibility\nReferenced from function pointer table at 0x6fa0f96f",
