      "name": "BuildColonSeparatedStringList",
      "signature": "undefined1 * BuildColonSeparatedStringList(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined1 *",
      "comment": "Build colon-separated string list from global data pairs\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load global pointer from PTR_PTR_00413198 (0x413198)\n  2. Loop 1: Calculate total buffer size needed\n     - Iterate 12 (0xc) items\n     - Sum strlen of two string fields per item\n     - Add 2 bytes per item for colons (0x3a)\n  3. Allocate memory for concatenated string + null terminator\n  4. Loop 2: Concatenate strings with colons\n     - For each of 12 items:\n       * Write colon\n       * Copy first string field\n       * Write colon\n       * Copy second string field\n     - Null-terminate result\n  5. Return allocated buffer pointer\n\nParameters: None (uses global PTR_PTR_00413198)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Pointer to allocated string buffer with colon-separated pairs\n       NULL if malloc fails (size == 0 fallback in caller)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns NULL if malloc allocation fails\n  - Accesses global structure at fixed offset (0x413198)\n  - Assumes 12 item records exist in global data array",
