      "name": "ShutdownMcpClient",
      "signature": "int ShutdownMcpClient(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Shuts down the MCP (Multiplayer Control Protocol) client connection.\n\nClassification: Cleanup function - Called during multiplayer UI shutdown sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call D2MCPCLIENT.Ordinal_10054 to perform primary MCP shutdown\n2. Call D2MCPCLIENT.Ordinal_10053(0) to finalize/reset MCP state\n3. Return 1 (TRUE) indicating successful shutdown\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating successful shutdown\n\nCallers:\n  - FUN_6fa10780: UI reset sequence (calls ResetButtonFrameStates first)\n  - Second caller at 0x6fa10b0b\n\nExternal Dependencies:\n  - D2MCPCLIENT.DLL Ordinal_10054: Primary MCP shutdown routine\n  - D2MCPCLIENT.DLL Ordinal_10053: MCP state reset (param 0 = full reset)\n\nNotes:\n  Simple cleanup wrapper that ensures MCP client resources are released\n  in proper order. Called as part of Battle.net UI teardown.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.03",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:07373469c33a8e04f52abab7b9f69d1b2e02e3144235cc043334047e0ffc2b21",
