      "name": "IncrementBnetMaxPlayers",
      "signature": "int IncrementBnetMaxPlayers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Increments the maximum players count in Battle.net game creation UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Unicode text from max players edit box via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n2. Convert Unicode string to UTF-8 (max 5 characters) into stack buffer\n3. Call FUN_6fa138ab to parse/increment the numeric value\n4. Format the incremented value back into a string buffer\n5. Convert result to Unicode and update the edit box control\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function - operates on global UI controls)\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 indicating success\n\nGlobals Referenced:\ng_pBnetMaxPlayersLabel - Pointer to max players edit box control\ng_szFormatBuffer - Temporary string buffer for formatting (at 0x6fa1daec)\nszFmtNumber - Format string for numeric conversion\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction body boundaries are broken (1 byte only). Decompiler output was captured from prior analysis showing complete function behavior.\n\nClassification: Internal utility - UI event handler for max players increment button",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.03",
