      "name": "SkipChannelNamePrefix",
      "signature": "char * SkipChannelNamePrefix(char * lpszChannelName)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Extracts channel name by skipping the asterisk prefix marker.\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Leaf utility - string parsing helper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search for asterisk (*) character (0x2A) in input string using strchr\n2. If asterisk not found, return original string unchanged\n3. If asterisk found but next character is null terminator, return original string\n4. Otherwise return pointer to character immediately after asterisk\n\nParameters:\n  lpszChannelName (ECX) - Input string potentially prefixed with \"*ChannelName\"\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to character after asterisk if valid prefix found\n          Original string pointer if no asterisk or asterisk at end\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n  - NULL result from strchr returns original string\n  - Asterisk at string end (e.g., \"name*\") returns original string\n  - Multiple asterisks only skips first one\n\nUSAGE CONTEXT:\n  Battle.net channel names use asterisk prefix for channel type indicators.\n  This function strips the prefix to get the actual channel/user name.\n  Called by ProcessChatCommandAndUIMessage to extract whisper targets.\n  Called by profile panel functions to parse channel member names.\n\nMAGIC NUMBERS:\n  0x2A - ASCII asterisk '*' character",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
