      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resets the profile edit panel UI and restores default input handling.\n\nCalled when exiting profile editing mode (33 callers across UI initialization/reset functions).\n\nClassification: Cleanup function - tears down profile editing state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwProfileEditState - if 0, skip cleanup and go to step 5\n2. If state == 1 (edit mode): dispatch handlers for profile edit items 1-6\n3. If state != 1 (creation mode): dispatch handlers for profile creation controls\n   (unknown object, name display, location, age, description, bio, input item)\n4. Reset g_dwProfileEditState to 0, dispatch handlers for common labels and buttons\n5. Set current input to g_apBnetUIObjects[10] (default input control)\n6. Call RestoreDefaultInputPointer to restore standard input handling\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwProfileEditState: Reset to 0\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called from 17+ UI reset/initialization functions\n- Part of Battle.net multiplayer UI cleanup sequence\n- Ensures profile panel state is cleared before UI transitions",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
