      "name": "ConvertCharacterToLowerCase",
      "signature": "uint ConvertCharacterToLowerCase(uint dwCharacter)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Convert ASCII uppercase character to lowercase with locale support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale functionality is available via g_dwLocaleAvailableFlag\n2. If locale not available, perform simple ASCII conversion:\n   - Validate character is in range 0x41-0x5A (A-Z)\n   - Add 0x20 to convert to lowercase (a-z)\n3. If locale is available, use critical section protection:\n   - Increment g_dwCriticalSectionCounter using InterlockedIncrement\n   - Check if critical section limit exceeded (g_dwCriticalSectionLimit != 0)\n   - If limit exceeded, enter critical section via FUN_6ff2c3fe(0x13)\n   - Call locale-aware conversion function FUN_6ff2bdda with context and character\n   - Exit critical section appropriately based on lock state\n4. Return converted character or original if no conversion needed\n\nParameters:\ndwCharacter (uint): ASCII character code to convert to lowercase (0-255)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Converted lowercase character code, or original character if:\n  - Character is not uppercase letter (outside A-Z range)\n  - Locale conversion fails or is unavailable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Non-ASCII characters (> 127) depend on locale implementation\n- Critical section timeout handled by limit check mechanism\n- Function maintains thread safety through InterlockedIncrement/Decrement\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x40 (64): ASCII '@', one less than 'A' for range check\n0x5A (90): ASCII 'Z', upper bound for uppercase letters  \n0x5B (91): ASCII '[', one more than 'Z' for range check\n0x20 (32): Offset between uppercase and lowercase ASCII (A=65, a=97)\n0x13 (19): Critical section ID for locale operations\n\nError Handling:\n- Invalid character range: Returns original character unchanged\n- Critical section failure: Handled by Windows synchronization primitives\n- Locale function failure: Returns result from FUN_6ff2bdda (may be original)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
