      "name": "LaunchUrlInDefaultBrowser",
      "signature": "uint LaunchUrlInDefaultBrowser(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Opens a URL in the system's default web browser by querying the Windows registry\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get URL string from callback vtable at offset 0xB0\n2. Return 1 if URL is null (no URL to launch)\n3. Zero-initialize 0x800 byte buffer for file type association\n4. Get desktop window handle and bring to foreground\n5. Query HKCR\\.html for file type association\n6. Query HKCR\\<filetype>\\shell\\open\\command for browser path\n7. Append \" %1\" suffix and URL to command buffer using inline memcpy\n8. Initialize STARTUPINFO (cb=0x44) and call CreateProcessA\n9. On success: Close process and thread handles\n10. On failure: Display error UI via ValidateStringId(0x14DC)\n11. Clean up UI child elements and create fallback buttons\n12. Call cleanup callback at vtable offset 0x78\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function - URL obtained via vtable callback)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 regardless of success or failure\n  Success/failure is tracked internally via local flag\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  uStack_13ff - Buffer continuation for command template (0x400 bytes at ESP+0xC00)\n  uStack_7ff - Buffer continuation for file type data (0x800 bytes at ESP+0x400)\n  Note: These are decompiler artifacts from large stack buffers and cannot be typed\n\nGlobals:\n  g_pCallbackVtable - Callback vtable for URL retrieval (0xB0) and cleanup (0x78)\n  g_byInitFlag - Buffer initialization byte\n  g_nNumSubChildren - UI child element count (max 32, asserts if exceeded)\n  g_apSubChildrenArray - Array of child UI element pointers\n  g_dwInventorySubState - Inventory UI state, reset to 0 on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14DC - Error string ID for browser launch failure\n  0x20019 - KEY_READ registry access rights\n  0x20 - NORMAL_PRIORITY_CLASS for CreateProcessA\n  0x44 - sizeof(STARTUPINFOA)\n  0x1086 - Assert line number for max children check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
