      "name": "InitializeGameListDialog",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameListDialog(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the multiplayer game list dialog UI and populates game selection controls.\n\nClassification: Initialization function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame values for three button frames to initial state (value 0)\n2. Call helper functions FUN_6fa10090 and FUN_6fa0f490 for additional UI cleanup\n3. Dispatch inventory handlers to clear 10 inventory slots (g_dwInventorySlot1-10)\n4. Set current input item and pointer from global state\n5. Loop through sub-children array dispatching inventory handlers, then reset count\n6. Reset inventory sub-state and extra state globals to 0\n7. Call FUN_6fa117b0 for intermediate cleanup\n8. Dispatch handlers for remaining inventory slots (9 and 10)\n9. If special mode flag is 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n10. Reset inventory panel mode from 3 to 0 if applicable\n11. Set/clear bit mask on inventory panel state if non-null\n12. Create UI factory objects for dialog elements:\n    - Panel object from g_GameListPanelFactory\n    - Game name text box from g_GameNameTextBoxFactory (string ID 0x148D)\n    - Password text box from g_PasswordTextBoxFactory (string ID 0x148E)\n    - Max players text box from g_MaxPlayersTextBoxFactory (string ID 0x148F)\n    - Join button from g_JoinButtonFactory\n    - Scrollbar from g_GameListScrollbarFactory\n    - Edit control from g_GameNameEditFactory\n13. Configure edit control with max length 0x20, callbacks at 0x6fa02df0 and 0x6fa05490\n14. Get game list string from callback vtable and process:\n    - Compare strings at offsets 0x379 and 0x359 from g_pGameListData\n    - If different, use the appropriate string for the scrollbar\n    - Iterate through null-terminated string list adding unique entries\n15. Get default game name from FUN_6fa0b4b0 and set in edit control\n16. Initialize screenshot config and scroll to index 0\n17. Check if edit box has content by converting Unicode to Win string\n    - If string length > 0, set bit mask to 1 (enable join button)\n18. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nNumSubChildren - Reset to 0\n  g_dwInventorySubState - Reset to 0\n  g_dwInventoryExtraState - Reset to 0\n  g_dwInventoryPanelMode - Reset from 3 to 0 if applicable\n  g_dwInventorySlot1-10 - Cleared via inventory handlers\n  Multiple slot globals - Set to factory-created objects\n\nString IDs:\n  0x148D - Game name label text\n  0x148E - Password label text\n  0x148F - Max players label text\n\nCallbacks:\n  0x6fa02df0 - Edit field value change callback\n  0x6fa05490 - Edit data field 9B callback\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, extra initialization via FUN_6fa127f0\n  - If edit box is empty, join button mask set to 0 (disabled)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
