      "name": "EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI",
      "signature": "int EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI(int nGameListData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the Battle.net multiplayer user interface and establishes connection state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Record start timestamp for elapsed time calculation\n2. Initialize music system state and shutdown existing sound\n3. Validate game list data pointer at offset 0x21d; assert on null\n4. Call virtual function at +0x74 to verify connection; exit with state 4 on failure\n5. Load all Battle.net front-end cel images (buttons, dialogs, textboxes, realm UI)\n6. Create 11 UI slot elements at 0x3c byte stride for character selection\n7. Clear 10 character name slots (0x100 bytes each)\n8. Reset inventory panels and set default input focus\n9. Release 8 UI control handles and previously allocated game list entries\n10. Initialize Unicode string buffer (512 entries) for player name display\n11. Build concatenated game name from linked list entries if session exists\n12. Create password and description input controls\n13. Check expansion flags (offset 0x1ea) for expansion-specific initialization\n14. Check realm type (offset 0x356); enable ladder mode if type equals 4\n15. Verify expansion MPQ exists if in expansion mode\n16. Format realm info string with game name and character data\n17. Attempt game entry via virtual function call at +0x74\n18. Process message pump and update UI elements\n19. Cleanup: Release all cel images, reset music state, restore MCP connection\n20. Calculate and log elapsed time\n\nParameters:\nnGameListData (ECX) - Pointer to game list context structure containing:\n                      +0x21d: Connection handle pointer (must be non-null)\n                      +0xb8: Character info block\n                      +0x225: Password string\n                      +0x1ea: Expansion flags (bit 3: expansion, bit 4: ladder)\n                      +0x356: Realm type (4 = ladder realm)\n                      +0x359: Additional realm data\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns success; actual connection state stored in g_dwMultiplayerState\n    State values: 0=idle, 3=connecting, 4=connection failed/disconnected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer at offset 0x21d triggers FogAssert with file/line info\n- Virtual function +0x74 returning 0 sets state to 4 (disconnected)\n- Expansion flag check at 0x6fa3e9cc determines whether to call expansion init\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x690 - Stack frame size (1680 bytes)\n0x3c - UI slot element stride (60 bytes)\n0x100 - Character name buffer size (256 bytes)\n0x200 - Unicode buffer entry count (512)\n0x17d4 - Pool allocation size for game list cleanup\n\nOrdinal Calls:\nOrdinal_10052 - SetMusicTrack: Sets current music track ID\nOrdinal_10053 - StopMusic: Stops current music playback\nOrdinal_10054 - SetStringTableIndex: Sets active string table for UI text\nOrdinal_10048 - InitStringTable: Initializes string table for localization\nOrdinal_10049 - LoadStringTable: Loads string table from MPQ\nOrdinal_10001 - GetUnitRoom: Gets room context for unit display",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
