      "name": "UpdatePanelDisplayState",
      "signature": "int UpdatePanelDisplayState(int nUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Updates panel display state by synchronizing display flags and decrementing state counter.\n\nClassification: Worker function - updates UI panel state variables\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy g_byPanelDisplayMode to first byte of g_byPanelDisplayFlags (sync current mode)\n2. Calculate new state: g_dwPanelStateA = g_dwPanelStateA - g_dwPanelStateDecrement\n3. Clamp result to zero if negative (using branchless: result & ((result < 1) - 1))\n4. Store clamped value back to g_dwPanelStateA\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (int) - Unused parameter, passed for callback compatibility (stdcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE/success)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_byPanelDisplayMode (0x6fa1b05c) - READ - Current panel display mode (byte)\n  g_byPanelDisplayFlags (0x6fa1b054) - WRITE - Panel display flags, first byte updated\n  g_dwPanelStateA (0x6fa1b058) - READ/WRITE - Panel state counter (uint)\n  g_dwPanelStateDecrement (0x6fa208e0) - READ - Decrement amount for state counter (uint)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_dwPanelStateA <= g_dwPanelStateDecrement, result is clamped to 0 (prevents underflow)\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (cleans 4 bytes from stack via RET 4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
