      "name": "PopulateLadderPanelEntries",
      "signature": "void PopulateLadderPanelEntries(uint dwStartIndex, int nEntryCount, int nEntryStride, byte byDisplayFlags, int * pLadderEntryData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Populates ladder panel entries with player ranking data or displays \"not on ladder\" message.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exit early if g_dwInventoryExtraState is null (panel not initialized)\n2. If nEntryCount == 0 (reset/error mode):\n   a. Initialize three 256-element Unicode buffers for message formatting\n   b. Get current profile character name via GetProfileCharacterName\n   c. Convert format string \"Player %s is not on ladder\" to Unicode\n   d. Format complete error message with player name\n   e. Reset Battle.net UI elements and clear panel slots 1-10\n   f. Dispatch handlers for all sub-children arrays\n   g. Clear inventory state flags and callback pointer\n   h. Handle special mode flag (g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1)\n   i. Reset panel mode 3 to 0 if active\n   j. Toggle bit mask on panel state object\n   k. Reset button frame values for navigation buttons\n   l. Create text box with formatted error message\n3. If byDisplayFlags matches g_byPanelDisplayFlags (populate mode):\n   a. Navigate scrollbar to dwStartIndex if g_dwPanelStateA == -1\n   b. Initialize character class name lookup array (7 classes)\n   c. Calculate end index: min(dwStartIndex + nEntryCount, g_szCommandBufferEnd)\n   d. For each entry from dwStartIndex to end index:\n      - Extract flags dword from pLadderEntryData[2]\n      - Extract class index (bits 0-3), difficulty (bits 8-12), level (bits 16-23)\n      - Compare entry name against g_szPanelDisplayText (current player)\n      - Set line color: 0 for match, 4 or 5 for others based on flag bit 4\n      - Clear text line and set color\n      - Format 1-based rank number to column 0\n      - Get character title via CalculateCharacterTitleTier\n      - Concatenate title + player name to column 1\n      - Set class abbreviation from lookup array to column 2\n      - Format level to column 3\n      - Format experience as abbreviated number to column 4\n      - Advance entry pointer by nEntryStride + 12 bytes\n\nParameters:\n  dwStartIndex (ECX, uint): Starting row index in ladder panel (0-based)\n  nEntryCount (EDX, int): Number of entries to populate; 0 triggers reset mode\n  nEntryStride (Stack+0x4, int): Byte stride between entries beyond 12-byte header\n  byDisplayFlags (Stack+0x8, byte): Display flags that must match g_byPanelDisplayFlags\n  pLadderEntryData (Stack+0xC, int*): Pointer to ladder entry data array\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nLadder Entry Structure (at pLadderEntryData):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     dwExpLow        Experience points (low dword of 64-bit value)\n  0x04    4     dwExpHigh       Experience points (high dword of 64-bit value)\n  0x08    4     dwFlags         Character flags bitfield\n  0x0C    N     szPlayerName    Null-terminated player name string\n\nFlag Bits in dwFlags (offset 0x08):\n  Bits 0-3   (0x0F):   Character class index (0-6)\n  Bit 4      (0x10):   Unknown flag (affects line color selection)\n  Bit 5      (0x20):   Expansion character flag (Lord of Destruction)\n  Bit 6      (0x40):   Hardcore character flag\n  Bits 8-12  (0x1F00): Difficulty level (shifted >> 8)\n  Bits 16-23 (0xFF0000): Character level (shifted >> 16)\n\nCharacter Class Mapping:\n  0 = Amazon (ama)\n  1 = Sorceress (sor)\n  2 = Necromancer (nec)\n  3 = Paladin (pal)\n  4 = Barbarian (bar)\n  5 = Druid (dru)\n  6 = Assassin (ass)\n\nText Panel Columns:\n  Column 0: Rank number (1-based)\n  Column 1: Character title + player name\n  Column 2: Class abbreviation (3 chars)\n  Column 3: Character level\n  Column 4: Experience (abbreviated format, e.g., \"1.2M\")\n\nLine Color Values:\n  0: Current player highlight (name matches g_szPanelDisplayText)\n  4: Standard entry (flag bit 4 clear)\n  5: Alternate entry (flag bit 4 set)\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_dwInventoryExtraState: Panel state pointer (must be non-null)\n  g_byPanelDisplayFlags: Current display mode flags\n  g_dwPanelStateA: Scroll position state (-1 = needs positioning)\n  g_szCommandBufferEnd: Maximum entry count limit\n  g_szPanelDisplayText: Current player name for highlighting\n  g_dwSpecialModeFlag: Special UI mode indicator\n  g_dwInventoryPanelMode: Panel mode state (3 = needs reset)\n  g_pInventoryPanelState: Panel state object for bit mask operations\n\nCalled By:\n  ResetInventoryPanelToInitialState, ResetInventoryPanelAndShowSelection,\n  ResetInventoryPanelAndUIState, ResetInventoryPanelAndSubChildren,\n  InitializePanelDisplayDefault, InitializeOrResetInventoryPanel,\n  InitializePanelMode2, InitializeOrResetCharSelPanel",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
