      "comment": "Resets all panel button states and initializes the character class selection list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame values for panel slots 1-6 to disabled state (0)\n2. If g_dwPanelResetFlag is set, also reset slots 7-8\n3. Set slot 8 to enabled state (1) - active selection slot\n4. Early exit if g_byPanelDisplayFlags is 0x10 or 0x07 (specific panel modes)\n5. Set command buffer end to 200 (0xC8)\n6. Clear the text data list for inventory extra state\n7. Initialize 2 Unicode objects on stack via default constructor\n8. Call FUN_6fa12b5e to copy string from character class abbreviations table\n9. Convert ANSI to Unicode via win2Unicode\n10. Add converted text lines to inventory state panel with width 200, color 4\n11. Navigate scrollbar to index 0\n12. Set g_nPanelScrollOffset to -2 (0xFFFFFFFE)\n13. Set g_fClassListEnabled to 1 (enabled)\n14. Calculate display mode offset based on g_byPanelDisplayFlags range:\n    - Range [0,7]: offset = 0, result = 7\n    - Range [9,16]: offset = 9, result = 16 (0x10)\n    - Range [19,26]: offset = 19 (0x13), result = 26 (0x1A)\n    - Range [27,34]: offset = 27 (0x1B), result = 34 (0x22)\n    - Out of range: Assert failure with FogAssert\n15. Store offset+7 to g_byPanelDisplayFlags and clear g_dwPanelStateA\n16. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nLocal Variables (SSA temporaries):\n- cVar1 (byModeOffset): Calculated display mode offset based on range check\n- uVar2 (dwDisplayFlags): Zero-extended g_byPanelDisplayFlags for range comparison\n- iVar3 (nLoopCounter): Loop counter for Unicode constructor calls (2 iterations)\n- local_4 (awszClassAbbrev): Stack buffer for Unicode class abbreviation (4 wchars)\n- acStack_6 (szClassAbbrev): Stack buffer for ANSI class abbreviation (2 chars)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit for display flags 0x10 or 0x07 without modifying class list\n- Assert failure triggers FUN_6fa12bdd(-1) which does not return\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_dwPanelStateSlot1-8: Panel button state handles\n- g_dwPanelResetFlag: Controls whether slots 7-8 are reset\n- g_byPanelDisplayFlags: Current panel display mode (byte)\n- g_szCommandBufferEnd: Text width setting (set to 200)\n- g_dwInventoryExtraState: Text list control handle\n- g_nPanelScrollOffset: Scroll position (-2 initial)\n- g_fClassListEnabled: Class list availability flag\n- g_dwPanelStateA: Panel state cleared to 0\n\nSource: C:\\Projects\\Diablo2\\Source\\D2Multi\\Src\\ChatDlg.cpp line 5623 (0x15F7)",
