      "name": "OnBnetChannelJoined",
      "signature": "int OnBnetChannelJoined(int nUnused, char * lpszChannelName)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Battle.net channel join callback - handles the event when user joins a channel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format \"You have joined channel: %s\" message with channel name\n2. Initialize Unicode buffer array (576 elements, 1152 bytes)\n3. Convert ANSI message to Unicode\n4. Validate Unicode string length < 500, assert if exceeded\n5. Get string ID 0xF9A via ValidateStringId (returns pattern to strip)\n6. Strip all occurrences of pattern from message (removes special markers)\n7. Add formatted message to chat text box with style 5 (system message)\n8. Copy channel name to g_pGameListHead global buffer (inline strcpy)\n9. Copy channel name to g_pGameListData+0x359 (game list channel field)\n10. If g_pGameListData+0x379 is empty, copy channel name there too\n11. Loop through g_apGameSlotButtons array, set bit 1 on each button\n12. Clear bit mask on g_pScrollListControl\n13. Call ResetBnetGameListAndButtonStates to reset game list UI\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused - Unused parameter (callback signature requirement)\n  lpszChannelName - ANSI string of the joined channel name\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_pGameListData - Pointer to game list data structure\n  g_pGameListHead - Channel name storage buffer\n  g_apGameSlotButtons - Array of 11 game slot button pointers (ends at 0x6fa21728)\n  g_pScrollListControl - Scroll list UI control pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Unicode length assertion at line 0x2E4 in ComCallback.cpp\n  - Pattern stripping only occurs if pattern found AND not at string end\n  - Channel name copied to backup field only if currently empty\n\nClassification: Callback Handler - invoked from function pointer table at 0x6fa1d7b8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
