      "name": "FormatAndDisplayChatMessage",
      "signature": "int FormatAndDisplayChatMessage(char * lpszPlayerName, char * lpszMessageText)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "FormatAndDisplayChatMessage - Formats and displays a chat message in the text box\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse player name to extract name and title components via ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle\n2. Search global player list (g_pPlayerListHead) for matching player entry\n3. Check player flags (0x90 offset) for special status:\n   - Flag 0x2: Set color mode to 0 (no color)\n   - Flag 0x1 or 0x8: Set color mode to 3 (special color)\n   - Default: Color mode 4 (normal)\n4. Format message based on player name availability:\n   - With name+title: Format as \"%s%s\" (name concatenated with title)\n   - With name only: Copy name directly\n   - Format final as \"<%s> \" (angle brackets around name)\n   - No name: Format message text directly\n5. Convert ANSI strings to Unicode using win2Unicode\n6. Validate string length (max 500 characters)\n7. Apply profanity filter by searching for patterns (StringId 0xF9A) and removing matches\n8. Apply color codes:\n   - Prepend primary color code to message\n   - Append secondary color code\n9. Concatenate filtered message portion\n10. Display final formatted message via CharSelectTextBoxAddText\n\nParameters:\n  lpszPlayerName - ANSI string containing the player's display name (may be NULL)\n  lpszMessageText - ANSI string containing the chat message content\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE) on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL or empty player name: Message displayed without player prefix\n  - Empty player title: Only name portion used in format\n  - Player flags 0x2: Disables color formatting\n  - Player flags 0x1/0x8: Uses special color mode 3\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4 - Default primary color mode\n  0x3 - Special player color mode\n  0xD0C - Stack frame size (3340 bytes for buffers)\n  0x240 - Unicode buffer size (576 wchars = 1152 bytes)\n  0x1F4 - Maximum string length (500 chars)\n  0xF9A - Profanity filter string ID\n  0x90 - Player flags offset in entry structure\n  0xA0 - Next pointer offset in player list entry\n\nError Handling:\n  - Calls FogAssert if string exceeds 500 characters\n  - Calls ReportError(-1) for fatal errors",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
