      "name": "InitializeGameListPanelControls",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameListPanelControls(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes UI controls for the Battle.net game list panel.\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up game creation/join UI components\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate game list data via GetGameListDataPointer()\n2. If data unavailable (-1), show error dialog (string 0x1413) and return\n3. Check MCP client status via IsMcpClientActive()\n4. If MCP active, delegate to InitializeMotdPanelControls() and return\n5. Clear game status flag at offset 0x20B in game data structure\n6. Create main UI controls using CreateObjectByTypeFactory():\n   - Header textbox, content textbox, cancel/create/join buttons\n   - Game name, password, and difficulty input fields\n7. Configure input field properties:\n   - Game name: max 16 chars, validation callback at 0x6fa104a0\n   - Password: max 16 chars, validation callback at 0x6fa10540\n   - Description: max 32 chars\n8. Check expansion mode and branch:\n   a. Expansion mode:\n      - Create max players controls and toggle button\n      - Link input fields: Name->Password->Difficulty->MaxPlayers->MaxPlayersInput->Name\n      - Query registry for LvlRest and MaxPlayer settings\n      - Apply saved values or set defaults\n   b. Non-expansion mode:\n      - Create difficulty buttons with disabled state\n      - Link input fields: Name->Password->Difficulty->Name\n9. Query registry for DiffLevel setting\n10. Extract character level from game flags (bits 8-12)\n11. Configure difficulty buttons based on level requirements:\n    - Normal: requires level 4 (non-HC) or 5\n    - Nightmare: requires level 8 (non-HC) or 10\n    - Buttons disabled if requirements not met\n12. Set default difficulty if none pre-selected\n13. Set initial focus to game name input\n14. If expansion, call UpdateMaxPlayersToggleState()\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (modifies global UI control state)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dwPad_6fa3e8ec (0x6fa3e8ec): First textbox control\n- g_pMotdHeaderTextBox (0x6fa3e8f0): Header textbox\n- g_pMotdContentTextBox (0x6fa3e8f4): Content textbox\n- g_pBnetGameCancelButton (0x6fa3e8f8): Cancel button\n- g_pBnetGameCreateButton (0x6fa3e8fc): Create button\n- g_pBnetGameJoinButton (0x6fa3e900): Join button\n- g_pMaxPlayersTextBox1 (0x6fa3e904): Max players label 1\n- g_pMaxPlayersTextBox2 (0x6fa3e908): Max players label 2\n- g_pBnetGameNameLabel (0x6fa3e92c): Game name input\n- g_pBnetPasswordLabel (0x6fa3e930): Password input\n- g_pBnetDifficultyLabel (0x6fa3e934): Difficulty input\n- g_pBnetMaxPlayersLabel (0x6fa3e938): Max players input (expansion)\n- g_pMaxPlayersInputField (0x6fa3e93c): Max players entry\n- g_pMaxPlayersToggleButton (0x6fa3e940): Toggle button\n- g_nDifficultyLevel (0x6fa3e9dc): Selected difficulty level\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1413 (5139): Error string for unavailable game list\n- 0x141E (5150): Header label string ID\n- 0x149A (5274): Content label string ID\n- 0x1488-148C (5256-5260): Button text string IDs\n- 0x271F-2721 (10015-10017): Difficulty level strings\n- 0x29A (666): Special value indicating no level restriction\n\nRegistry Keys:\n- \"Diablo II\" / \"LvlRest\": Level restriction setting\n- \"Diablo II\" / \"MaxPlayer\": Max players setting (1-8)\n- \"Diablo II\" / \"DiffLevel\": Saved difficulty level (0=Easy, 1=Normal, 2=Nightmare)\n\nLevel Requirements (character level from flags bits 8-12):\n- Normal difficulty: Level >= 4 (non-hardcore) or >= 5 (any mode)\n- Nightmare difficulty: Level >= 8 (non-hardcore) or >= 10 (any mode)\n- Bit 5 (0x20) in flags indicates hardcore mode\n\nCallers:\n- InitializeBnetPanelState: Called during Battle.net panel initialization",
