      "name": "HandleCreateGameButtonClick",
      "signature": "bool HandleCreateGameButtonClick(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Handles the Create Game button click in Battle.net multiplayer UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate button state via IsButtonValid\n2. Get game name from edit box via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n3. If game name empty, exit early (returns false via RET 0x4)\n4. Get password and description from edit boxes\n5. Check expansion mode via GetUnitBitMask\n6. If expansion: get max players and difficulty settings\n7. Build game creation string with title case formatting\n8. Validate string ID and copy to ANSI buffer\n9. Set game flags including ladder mode and difficulty\n10. Initialize game join session data\n11. Reset Bnet UI elements and show MOTD panel\n12. If MCP client active, shutdown connection\n13. Return true on success\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nbool - TRUE (1) on successful game creation initiation\n     - FALSE (0) on validation failure (button invalid or empty game name)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit at 0x6fa107c1 if button validation fails\n- Early exit at 0x6fa10808 if game name length < 1\n- Expansion mode (checked via GetUnitBitMask) enables additional options\n\nPhantom Variables:\n- szGameNameBytes (undefined1[511]): Assembly-only stack buffer at [ESP+0x68]\n  Used for game name ANSI conversion, no HighVariable - cannot set type via MCP\n\nOrdinal Calls:\n- Ordinal_10052 @ 0x6fa10b15: ShutdownMcpClient - Closes MCP connection if active\n- Ordinal_10002: Referenced via callee (not directly in function body)",
