      "name": "InitializeInventoryPanel",
      "signature": "int InitializeInventoryPanel(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes the inventory panel UI by resetting button states and creating child UI objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame values for 3 primary buttons to 0\n2. Call FUN_6fa10090() and FUN_6fa0f490() for additional initialization\n3. Dispatch inventory item handlers for slots 1-8\n4. Set current input item and pointer from globals\n5. Loop through existing sub-children array, dispatching handlers for each\n6. Reset g_nNumSubChildren counter to 0\n7. Reset inventory sub-state and extra-state to 0\n8. Call FUN_6fa117b0() for additional state reset\n9. Dispatch handlers for inventory slots 9-10\n10. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, call FUN_6fa127f0()\n11. If g_dwInventoryPanelMode == 3, reset it to 0\n12. If g_pInventoryPanelState is non-null, set bit mask 1\n13. Create 7 child UI objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory:\n    - Each creation checks g_nNumSubChildren < 32 (0x1f), asserts if exceeded\n    - Objects stored in g_apSubChildrenArray at current index\n    - g_nNumSubChildren incremented after each creation\n14. Add text to second created object via TextBoxAddTextWithDefaults (string ID 0x14c5)\n15. Set final created object as current input item\n16. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 indicating successful initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if g_nNumSubChildren exceeds 31 (max children limit)\n  - Panel mode 3 is cleared to 0 during initialization\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1f (31) - Maximum allowed sub-children count\n  0x14c5 (5317) - String resource ID for textbox content\n  0x1086 (4230) - Source file line number for assertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.08",
