      "name": "InsertTextBoxInSortedList",
      "signature": "void InsertTextBoxInSortedList(void * this, void * pTextBoxNode, char * pTextContent)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Inserts or updates a text box node in the global linked list, maintaining sorted order by pointer address. Allocates new node if not found, copies text content, and triggers UI rendering.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Search global list (DAT_6fa0a0f0) for existing node matching pTextBoxNode pointer\\n2. If found at any position, jump to copy_text_content to update existing node\\n3. If not found, allocate new 0x1b21-byte node via AllocateMemoryWithTracking\\n4. Store pTextBoxNode pointer at offset +0x200 in new node\\n5. Determine insertion position by comparing pointers with existing list entries\\n6. If list empty, insert as new head\\n7. If pTextBoxNode < head.pointer, insert before head and update DAT_6fa0a0f0\\n8. Otherwise, iterate through list to find correct position where pTextBoxNode fits in ascending order\\n9. Insert new node by updating next pointers (+0x204) to maintain sorted order\\n10. Copy pTextContent to new node buffer via _strncpy (maximum 0x200 bytes)\\n11. Null-terminate copied text at offset +0x200\\n12. Call RenderGameInterfaceTextBox to update UI display\\n13. Return (callee pops 4-byte parameter via RET 0x4)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pTextBoxNode (ECX): Base pointer to text box object/context being inserted\\n  pTextContent (EDX/stack): String buffer containing text to display (max 0x200 bytes)\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void (no return value)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Duplicate nodes: If pTextBoxNode already exists in list, only text is updated\\n  - List empty: Node becomes both head and tail when list is empty\\n  - Allocation size: Always allocates fixed 0x1b21 bytes (6945 bytes) for each node\\n  - Text buffer: Data copied via strncpy with 0x200-byte limit; manually null-terminated\\n  - Sorted order: Nodes maintained in ascending order by pointer value at offset +0x200\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\\n  +0x200  4     pNodePointer      void*     Pointer identifying this text box node\\n  +0x204  4     pNextNode         void*     Pointer to next node in sorted list (NULL=end)\\n  +0x000  512   szTextBuffer      char[512] Text content buffer\\n  +0x200  1     szNull            char      Null terminator at end of text",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
