      "name": "ConvertBytesToHexString",
      "signature": "void ConvertBytesToHexString(byte * pInputBuffer, uint * pOverflowFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts 16 bytes to hexadecimal string representation with overflow detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output flags to zero and set up loop parameters\n2. For each 16-byte block (2 iterations):\n   a. Load byte pair from input buffer\n   b. Look up values in lookup table at 0x6f9e8010\n   c. Calculate combined hex value: (lookup[byte[-1]] * 24) + lookup[byte[0]]\n   d. Check if overflow (>= 0x100) and set overflow flag bit if needed\n   e. Extract high nibble (>>4 & 0xF) and convert to ASCII hex ('0'-'F')\n   f. Extract low nibble (&0xF) and convert to ASCII hex ('0'-'F')\n   g. Store two ASCII hex characters to output buffer\n   h. Shift overflow mask left by 4 bits for next pair\n3. Advance to next 8-byte chunk and repeat\n\nParameters:\n- pInputBuffer (EAX): Pointer to input bytes; incremented by 1 at start\n- pOverflowFlags (EDI): Pointer to overflow status word; bits indicate which byte pairs overflowed\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Lookup table at 0x6f9e8010 provides pre-calculated values for byte-to-hex conversion\n- Overflow detection: If combined value >= 0x100, subtract 0x100 and set bit in status word\n- Each byte pair sets a different bit in overflow flags (bits 0-3 for 4 pairs)\n- Hex digit conversion: values 0-9 become '0'-'9' (add 0x30), values A-F become 'A'-'F' (add 0x37)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b01194e9e10db4c9169b176e38d63f04b2e49b96b94a4a35553dc46ba517d47c",
