      "comment": "Displays a security error message and terminates the application.\\n\\nThis function is called when runtime security checks fail (buffer overruns, unknown security failures, etc.). It builds an error message containing the program name and description, displays it via MessageBox, and exits with code 3.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if custom exception handler (DAT_6f9ebde0) is registered\\n2. If handler exists, call it; otherwise build standard error message\\n3. Determine error type (1=buffer overrun, other=unknown security failure)\\n4. Get module filename using GetModuleFileNameA\\n5. Validate message buffer size (must be <= 0x3c bytes for program name)\\n6. If necessary, truncate path and append \\\"...\\\" to fit buffer\\n7. Build complete error message by concatenating error type description, program name, and detailed error explanation\\n8. Display MessageBox with compiled error message\\n9. Call exit(3) to terminate with code 3\\n\\nParameters:\\n- errorCode (int): Error type code (1=buffer overrun detected, other=unknown security failure)\\n\\nReturns:\\n- void (never returns; calls exit(3) at end)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- GetModuleFileNameA may fail, uses \\\"&lt;program_name_unknown&gt;\\\" placeholder\\n- Path length validation ensures program name fits in 0x3c byte buffer; truncates with \\\"...\\\" if needed\\n- Uses SEH (Structured Exception Handling) prologue for exception safety\\n- Security cookie validation via XOR with stored value at [0x6f9e91f0]",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:6829c7e2ecf5617d1af04a2d6d84fcdc",
