      "name": "RenderTextBoxIfEnabled",
      "signature": "int RenderTextBoxIfEnabled(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Renders a text box if a global rendering flag is enabled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global render enabled flag from DAT_6fa0a0c8\n2. Test if the flag is zero (rendering disabled)\n3. If flag is zero, jump to return sequence (skip rendering)\n4. Push parameters for RenderTextBoxUnicodeText: text pointer (EAX), 0, 1\n5. Call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText to render the text box\n6. Move return value 1 into EAX (success indicator)\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses implicit EAX register for text pointer, global flag for control)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa0a0c8 is zero, the render call is skipped entirely (conditional execution)\n- The text pointer is expected to be in EAX when function is called\n- Return value is always 1 regardless of whether rendering occurred",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
