      "name": "InitializeGameStateAndDispatch",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameStateAndDispatch(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game state and dispatches command handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization flag (DAT_6fa09f28) is zero\n2. If flag is zero: Call ValidateAndSetStructureField, set flag to 1, generate random values\n3. Perform three consecutive random modulo checks (1000) with specific conditions\n4. If all conditions pass: Initialize 20 Unicode array elements and convert special string\n5. Check render flag and call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText with special text box ID (9)\n6. If initialization flag is non-zero: Reset flag to 0, call ValidateAndSetStructureField\n7. Call dispatch_command_handler to process pending commands\n8. Check render flag again and call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText with standard text box ID (11)\n9. Return 1 on all paths\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Random threshold values are checked modulo 1000 (0x3e8 in assembly)\n- Special Easter egg or debug condition requires three consecutive random value checks\n- Unicode array contains 20 elements (0x14 in assembly)\n- Two possible text rendering calls with different text box IDs (9=special, 11=standard)\n- Function manages global initialization state via DAT_6fa09f28 flag\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee cleanup (RET 0x4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:73481c31cc5d6dc8a2a32473b8a8d571",
