      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeEntityMode",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndInitializeEntityMode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates current entity mode state and initializes resources if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate current game entity mode states via ValidateGameEntityModes()\n2. Validate and set entity mode via ValidateAndSetEntityMode()\n3. Check if current mode (DAT_6f9e9c50) is not 0x0e (14) and not 0x05 (5)\n4. If mode check passes (initialization needed):\n   a. Set resource timeout to 200 (0xc8) at DAT_6fa08e4c\n   b. Call InitializeResourceState() to initialize game resources\n   c. Set initialization flag to 1 at DAT_6f9e9c40\n   d. Calculate inventory offset with parameter 5 via CalculateInventoryOffset()\n   e. Store offset result in DAT_6f9e9c50\n   f. Clear counter/state at DAT_6f9e9c54 to 0\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mode values 0x0e and 0x05 skip initialization (already initialized or in specific state)\n- Resource timeout is fixed at 200 units\n- The function always succeeds regardless of initialization path taken",
