      "name": "InitializeEntityModeAndInventory",
      "signature": "int InitializeEntityModeAndInventory(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes entity mode state and inventory offset calculation for non-special entity states.\n\nThis function validates the current entity mode and conditionally initializes resources when\nthe entity is not in special states 0x03 or 0x0c. It sets resource limits, calculates inventory\noffsets, and prepares entity state for normal gameplay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate current entity mode state through ValidateGameEntityModes()\n2. Attempt to set entity mode with parameter EDX=1 via ValidateAndSetEntityMode()\n3. Load current mode value from DAT_6f9e9c50\n4. Check if mode equals 0x0c (special dormant state) - skip initialization if true\n5. Check if mode equals 0x03 (special initialization state) - skip initialization if true\n6. Set resource limit DAT_6fa08e4c to 200 (0xc8)\n7. Call InitializeResourceState() to initialize entity resources\n8. Set initialization flag DAT_6f9e9c40 to 1\n9. Call CalculateInventoryOffset(3) to calculate inventory storage offset\n10. Store calculated offset in DAT_6f9e9c50\n11. Clear secondary state tracker DAT_6f9e9c54 to 0\n12. Return success code 1\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Function always succeeds and returns 1 (no error conditions)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Modes 0x03 and 0x0c are special entity states that skip initialization\n  - Mode 0x0c represents a dormant/dead state\n  - Mode 0x03 represents initial setup state\n  - Resource limit 200 (0xc8) is the standard entity resource cap\n  - Parameter 3 to CalculateInventoryOffset indicates standard 3-slot inventory",
