      "name": "InitializeEntityInventory",
      "signature": "int InitializeEntityInventory(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes entity inventory system with validation and resource setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ValidateGameEntityModes() to validate modes for all primary entities\n2. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode() with EDX=1 to ensure entity mode is initialized\n3. Load entity state byte from DAT_6f9e9c50\n4. If state equals 0x0B (skip marker), jump to return success\n5. If state equals 0x02 (skip marker), jump to return success\n6. Set resource limit DAT_6fa08e4c to 200 (0xC8)\n7. Call InitializeResourceState() to initialize resource tracking structures\n8. Set entity active flag DAT_6f9e9c40 to 1\n9. Call CalculateInventoryOffset(2) to calculate inventory offset with parameter 2\n10. Store returned offset value in DAT_6f9e9c50\n11. Clear inventory item count at DAT_6f9e9c54 to 0\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function operates on global entity state variables\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State values 0x0B and 0x02 skip initialization (already initialized)\n- Resource limit hardcoded to 200 items\n- Inventory offset calculation uses parameter 2 as base offset\n- Global flags and data at 0x6f9e9cXX control entity inventory state",
