      "signature": "int InitializeGameSession(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game session with entity validation and resource setup.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call ValidateGameEntityModes() to refresh all entity mode states\\n2. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode() with mode parameter from ECX\\n3. Load session state byte from global DAT_6f9e9c50\\n4. Check if state equals 0x0a or 0x01 (already initialized) - jump to success if true\\n5. Set timeout counter DAT_6fa08e4c to 0xc8 (200 ticks)\\n6. Call InitializeResourceState() to allocate and setup game resources\\n7. Set session active flag DAT_6f9e9c40 to 1\\n8. Call CalculateInventoryOffset(1) to compute offset for base 1\\n9. Store calculated offset as session state byte in DAT_6f9e9c50\\n10. Clear session state counter DAT_6f9e9c54 to 0\\n11. Return 1 (success)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - Function operates on global state and entity pointers\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Always returns 1 (success)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If session already initialized (state=0x0a or 0x01), skips resource allocation and jumps to success\\n- Timeout value 0xc8 (200) is a fixed hardcoded value for session duration\\n- Uses __stdcall convention with RET 0x4 for callee cleanup of 1 stack parameter\\n- Calling ValidateAndSetEntityMode with hardcoded ECX=1 parameter",
