      "name": "CreateLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "int CreateLinkedListNode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Create and initialize a new linked list node for game state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0xc17 (3095) bytes of memory using AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n2. Initialize first three fields to 0 and fourth field to 1\n3. Check if allocation succeeded (pointer non-null)\n4. If allocation failed, return 1 immediately\n5. If allocation succeeded, enter critical section for thread-safe list access\n6. Check if list head (DAT_6fa0a0e8) is null (empty list)\n7. If list has existing nodes, link new node to end: set previous tail's +0xc to new node\n8. Update list head or tail pointers accordingly\n9. Leave critical section\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global linked list management variables\n\nReturns:\nint - Success status (always returns 1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses critical section at 0x6fa08f00 for thread-safe multi-threaded access\n- Allocates 3095 bytes (0xc17) - specific size for game state structure\n- Fourth field initialized to 1 (possibly reference count or type indicator)\n- Maintains doubly-linked list with head and tail pointers\n- Global variables: DAT_6fa0a0e8 (head), DAT_6fa0a0ec (tail)",
