      "name": "UpdateEntityStatesAndCleanupUI",
      "signature": "int UpdateEntityStatesAndCleanupUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Updates entity validation states and cleans up UI controls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer from global address 0x6fa09158 into ECX and zero EDX\n2. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode to validate first entity state\n3. Load pointer from global address 0x6fa0915c into ECX and zero EDX\n4. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode to validate second entity state\n5. Load pointer from global address 0x6fa09150 into ECX and zero EDX\n6. Call ValidateAndSetEntityMode to validate third entity state\n7. Call FUN_6f9dbe00 to clean up UI controls and restore interface state\n8. Call ProcessInventoryInputDialog to handle inventory dialog state\n9. Return success status code 1\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global entity pointers and state variables\n\nReturns:\nint: Returns 1 indicating successful completion\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function uses three global data pointers at fixed addresses (0x6fa09158, 0x6fa0915c, 0x6fa09150) representing different entity objects in the game state. EDX is cleared to zero (second parameter set to 0) for each ValidateAndSetEntityMode call. Function performs cleanup operations sequentially before returning.",
