      "name": "InitializeGameStateSecondary",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameStateSecondary(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes secondary game state with command processing and validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global state flags and timers to default values\n2. Load peer address context from global memory (DAT_6fa09f14 + 0x229)\n3. If peer address field is not set:\n   - Call GetPeerAddress() to retrieve peer context\n   - If result is zero (valid peer):\n     - Dispatch command handler and get error code\n     - Call error handler with code and return address\n     - Return to caller\n4. Check if command buffer (DAT_6fa09f24) has space (< 0x20)\n5. If buffer has space:\n   - Process first command from DAT_6f9eb020 and store in command array\n   - Increment command buffer counter\n   - Check if buffer still has space for second command\n   - If yes: Process second command from DAT_6f9eb050 and store in array\n   - Dispatch command handler\n   - Render text to screen\n   - Initialize game state commands\n   - Initialize global state values with default parameters\n   - Return success to caller\n6. If buffer is full (>= 0x20):\n   - Get return address from stack frame offset 0x13e8\n   - Call cleanup and abort with error message and return address\n   - Call _exit(-1) for immediate termination\n\nReturns:\nvoid (function may return normally via early exit or abnormally via _exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If peer address check fails, function returns early\n- Command buffer has fixed size of 0x20 (32 slots)\n- Magic number 0x3e8 = 1000 (timeout/timer value)\n- Magic number 0x23 = 35 (state identifier)\n- Magic number 0x10 = 16 (configuration flag)\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n- DAT_6f9e9c44, DAT_6fa09fd4-0xf0, DAT_6fa0a03c cleared\n- DAT_6fa08e4c, DAT_6fa09f30, DAT_6f9e9c58, DAT_6fa09180, DAT_6fa08e48 set",
