      "name": "InitializeGameSession",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameSession(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a new game session by cleaning up previous state and resetting session variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CleanupUIControls to destroy UI elements from previous session\n2. Call InitializeGameStateVariables to reset all game state counters and flags\n3. Set game session mode flag (0x6f9e9c50) to 9 indicating active session\n4. Clear game session counter (0x6f9e9c54) to 0\n5. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nReturns:\n1 (success) - Game session initialized and ready for gameplay\n\nStructure Layout:\nSession state is stored in global variables:\n0x6f9e9c50: byte - Session mode flag (9=active, 0=inactive)\n0x6f9e9c54: dword - Session counter/index (reset to 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called once at game startup to prepare game state\n- Destroys all UI controls from previous sessions before initialization\n- Resets command processing state for new game input",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
