      "name": "FormatAndAppendTypeDecoration",
      "signature": "void FormatAndAppendTypeDecoration(uint outputType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Formats message type decoration string and appends it to destination buffer.\n\nThis function formats a type indicator based on the outputType parameter and appends it to a destination Unicode buffer (referenced by EBX). It allocates two local Unicode buffers: one for the main decoration (1024 elements), and one for the formatted type value (3 elements). The function validates that the final concatenated string does not exceed 500 characters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize typeDecorationBuffer (1024 Unicode elements) via loop with default constructors\n2. Initialize formattedTypeString (3 Unicode elements) via loop with default constructors\n3. Call dispatch_command_handler() to get template/prefix string\n4. Copy template string to typeDecorationBuffer via strcpy\n5. Format outputType parameter to ANSI string using wsprintfA with format string\n6. Convert formatted ANSI string to Unicode in formattedTypeString via toUnicode\n7. Concatenate formattedTypeString to typeDecorationBuffer via strcat\n8. Check if destinationBuffer is empty by testing word at [EBX] == 0\n9. If empty, copy typeDecorationBuffer to destinationBuffer and return\n10. If not empty, validate existing destinationBuffer length does not exceed 499 chars\n11. If validation fails (length >= 500), call CleanupAndAbort with error code\n12. If validation passes, concatenate typeDecorationBuffer to destinationBuffer via strcat\n13. Return via RET 0x4 (callee cleanup of 1 parameter)\n\nParameters:\noutputType (uint) - Message type code/flags passed from caller, formatted into type indicator string\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Formats and appends string to destinationBuffer (EBX), or aborts if buffer overflow detected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0x200 (512 decimal) is loop counter for 1024-element buffer initialization\n- Magic constant 0x3 (3 decimal) is loop counter for 3-element buffer initialization  \n- Magic constant 0xb60 (2912 decimal) is error ID passed to GetReturnAddress for abort\n- Magic constant 499 (0x1f4) is max string length validation threshold\n- Implicit parameter EBX contains pointer to destination Unicode buffer\n- Calling convention __stdcall uses EBX as implicit parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:49b10dee3fdfde684c3b5c6706b8f3f8",
