      "name": "ConvertStringToUnicodeAndRender",
      "signature": "int ConvertStringToUnicodeAndRender(char * pInputString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Converts an ANSI string to Unicode and renders it in a text box.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocates 0x480-byte (1152 Unicode characters) buffer on stack\\n2. Initializes entire Unicode buffer by calling constructor for each character (0x240 iterations of 2-byte increments)\\n3. Converts input ANSI string to Unicode format using win2Unicode function with 0x240 character limit\\n4. Checks if DAT_6fa0a0d4 resource state flag is set (non-zero indicates resources loaded)\\n5. If flag is set, calls ClearResourceState to reset rendering state\\n6. If flag is set, calls RenderTextBoxUnicodeText with parameters (3, 0, 0) to render text\\n7. Returns 1 (success code) to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\npInputString (char *): Pointer to null-terminated ANSI string to convert and render. Maximum 0x240 characters will be processed.\\n\\nReturns:\\nint: Always returns 1 (success code). No error checking on input validity.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Magic number 0x240 (576 decimal) is the Unicode buffer size in characters, requiring 0x480 (1152) bytes of stack space\\n- Entire Unicode buffer is zeroed via constructor calls before conversion\\n- Rendering only occurs if DAT_6fa0a0d4 flag is non-zero, allowing conditional text display\\n- Function does not validate input pointer or string length before conversion\\n- Stack allocation is large (1152 bytes) and may affect stack depth\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\noffset | size | name | type | description\\n-------|------|------|------|-------------\\n-0x480 | 1152 | unicodeBuffer | Unicode[1152] | Local Unicode character array for text conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:334d68fab8680f9ef3184fdb05bfdf23",
