      "name": "RenderTextMessage",
      "signature": "int RenderTextMessage(int textBoxId, char * pMessage)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Renders a UTF-8 encoded text message to a text box with Unicode conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the message string pointer from stack parameter 2\n2. Push constant 0x3 (indicating text box type or formatting mode)\n3. Push the message string pointer onto stack\n4. Call FUN_6f9dfc90 to convert UTF-8 to Unicode and render the text\n5. Move constant 1 into EAX (return value indicating success)\n6. Return to caller with 0x8 bytes of parameter cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  textBoxId (undefined4): Text box identifier or formatting mode flag\n  pMessage (char *): Pointer to null-terminated UTF-8 encoded message string\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success/true)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The constant 0x3 is passed to the rendering function and may indicate a specific text box type or formatting mode\n  - Function always returns success regardless of rendering results\n  - Message string is assumed to be valid and null-terminated",
