      "name": "CleanupUIControls",
      "signature": "int CleanupUIControls(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up and destroys all active UI controls and resets global UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Destroy UI control at 0x6fa09dbc (first UI element)\n2. Destroy UI control at 0x6fa09db0 (second UI element)\n3. Destroy UI control at 0x6fa09db4 (third UI element)\n4. Destroy UI control at 0x6fa09db8 (fourth UI element)\n5. Clear UI active state flag at 0x6fa09dc0 (set to 0)\n6. Load saved UI state from 0x6fa09160\n7. Restore global state with SetGlobalState()\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - 1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function assumes all four UI control pointers are valid and initialized\n- Global state value at 0x6fa09160 is pre-loaded before cleanup\n- Typically called during UI shutdown or panel closure",
